00:29:24.840 --> 00:29:27.480
Look at your brain, Kim.

00:29:27.520 --> 00:29:33.520
So you're wearing a 14 channel EEG
and this is just picking up electrical

00:29:33.560 --> 00:29:37.840
fluctuations that result from neurons
firing inside your brain.

00:29:37.880 --> 00:29:41.440
The brain is made up of billions
of neurons and when they interact,

00:29:41.480 --> 00:29:45.680
the chemical reaction just emits an
electrical impulse that we can pick up.

00:29:45.720 --> 00:29:50.120
You can see that different parts of your
brain is lighting up depending on what you

00:29:50.120 --> 00:29:53.720
might be thinking or whether you're
paying attention to what I am saying.

00:29:53.760 --> 00:29:56.360
So, what we're doing here is we're mapping

00:29:56.400 --> 00:30:02.120
those electrical fluctuations into a 3D
model of what your brain is doing and each

00:30:02.160 --> 00:30:06.440
of the colors represent a different
frequency band, which indicates how fast

00:30:06.480 --> 00:30:11.640
the information is traveling from one
part of the brain to another.

